<i>♪ Yo ♪</i>

21
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:16,045
<i>♪ Uh, move the world, move, move ♪</i>

22
00:01:16,128 --> 00:01:19,173
<i>♪ Now, look, if I step into the world
Let you have some fun ♪</i>

23
00:01:24,762 --> 00:01:25,679
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah ♪</i>

24
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:28,140
{\an8}<i>♪ Mmm-hmm, right ♪</i>

25
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
THE SHINY BLACK NOSE BEFORE ME

26
00:01:36,023 --> 00:01:38,776
[Legoshi growling]

27
00:01:45,074 --> 00:01:47,493
- [Seven trembling, whimpering]
- [heart beating]

28
00:01:47,618 --> 00:01:50,037
[growling]

29
00:01:51,205 --> 00:01:53,666
[suspenseful music playing]

30
00:01:58,087 --> 00:02:01,382
[sniffing, growling]

31
00:02:01,465 --> 00:02:03,634
[Seven] <i>He's going to kill me. I...</i>

32
00:02:04,385 --> 00:02:05,553
<i>I have to call someone.</i>

33
00:02:05,636 --> 00:02:07,596
[breathing heavily]

34
00:02:08,222 --> 00:02:11,475
- [straining]
- [Legoshi growling]

35
00:02:15,146 --> 00:02:18,357
[Legoshi] <i>Just calm down.
Control yourself.</i>

36
00:02:19,024 --> 00:02:20,693
Eat me, Legoshi!

37
00:02:20,776 --> 00:02:22,653
[Legoshi] <i>Living herbivore meat.</i>

38
00:02:24,363 --> 00:02:26,198
<i>Oh, it's too good to resist.</i>

39
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:29,076
[screaming]

40
00:02:33,873 --> 00:02:36,000
[straining]

41
00:02:36,083 --> 00:02:37,168
- [growls]
- [yelps]

42
00:02:37,251 --> 00:02:39,044
[Legoshi straining, breathing heavily]

43
00:02:39,128 --> 00:02:41,005
[Seven whimpering softly]

44
00:02:41,422 --> 00:02:43,465
[suspenseful music intensifies]

45
00:02:44,842 --> 00:02:46,343
{\an8}[Legoshi straining] Ms. Seven.

46
00:02:47,011 --> 00:02:49,221
[Legoshi breathing heavily]

47
00:02:54,518 --> 00:02:56,145
[music stops]

48
00:02:56,228 --> 00:02:57,104
[exhales]

49
00:02:57,813 --> 00:02:59,398
It is Ms. Seven, right?

50
00:02:59,481 --> 00:03:01,775
- [panting]
- Yes.

51
00:03:03,527 --> 00:03:04,486
My room...

52
00:03:06,155 --> 00:03:07,531
The electricity is out.

53
00:03:08,407 --> 00:03:09,658
What am I supposed to do?

54
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,746
[Seven stuttering]
You call the electric company, and...

55
00:03:13,829 --> 00:03:15,789
and tell them your address.

56
00:03:15,873 --> 00:03:17,666
[Legoshi] The electric company?

57
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:21,503
Yeah. Just tell them where you live,
and they can turn it on remotely.

58
00:03:22,129 --> 00:03:23,380
[grunts softly]

59
00:03:23,464 --> 00:03:24,298
Hmm?

60
00:03:25,341 --> 00:03:27,676
[amusing music playing]

61
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,094
Do you have a cellphone?

62
00:03:30,387 --> 00:03:32,890
You should be able
to find the number on Zoozle.

63
00:03:34,141 --> 00:03:35,351
I, uh...

64
00:03:36,435 --> 00:03:39,230
I canceled my contract
when I dropped out of school.

65
00:03:40,439 --> 00:03:41,273
What?

66
00:03:43,692 --> 00:03:48,822
[reading] <i>"World History,"
"Ocean Language," "GED Test Prep"?</i>

67
00:03:49,657 --> 00:03:51,116
Are you still a teenager?

68
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:57,039
Uh... I'm 17.
I'm working at an udon restaurant now.

69
00:03:57,831 --> 00:03:58,832
[Seven] Hmm.

70
00:04:04,838 --> 00:04:07,716
Your shoes are a little old-fashioned
for a teenager.

71
00:04:08,342 --> 00:04:12,763
Well, when you're a large carnivore,
you don't have a whole lot of options.

72
00:04:12,846 --> 00:04:15,266
Ah. Yeah, I suppose you're right.

73
00:04:15,933 --> 00:04:18,686
- Huh?
- You know, I actually work for that brand.

74
00:04:19,436 --> 00:04:21,188
Wha-- Is that right?

75
00:04:22,439 --> 00:04:23,857
Well, keep up the good work.

76
00:04:24,858 --> 00:04:26,110
[sighs]

77
00:04:26,193 --> 00:04:29,947
<i>Good. Small talk like this
helps keep my appetite at bay.</i>

78
00:04:31,073 --> 00:04:32,283
So, uh...

79
00:04:33,492 --> 00:04:35,995
Anyway, my name is Legoshi.

80
00:04:36,078 --> 00:04:38,080
Look, I'm sorry
I didn't introduce myself sooner.

81
00:04:38,163 --> 00:04:40,457
- Those scars...
- [Legoshi] Not like I wasn't in the mood.

82
00:04:40,541 --> 00:04:41,542
- [yelps]
- [Seven gasps]

83
00:04:41,625 --> 00:04:44,003
[yelping, breathing heavily]

84
00:04:44,086 --> 00:04:45,713
- Please don't touch me!
- What?

85
00:04:46,797 --> 00:04:47,631
Please.

86
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,843
[sighs]

87
00:04:52,052 --> 00:04:55,306
Well, I'll look up that number.
I can do that for you.

88
00:04:55,389 --> 00:04:57,391
[keypad clicking]

89
00:05:00,519 --> 00:05:01,645
Can I ask...

90
00:05:02,896 --> 00:05:06,608
I don't know if this is going to be
a weird thing for you to answer or not,

91
00:05:07,401 --> 00:05:11,280
but why are you staying here with me
instead of running?

92
00:05:12,323 --> 00:05:13,490
[Seven] Hmm?

93
00:05:15,326 --> 00:05:16,160
Hmm.

94
00:05:19,121 --> 00:05:23,167
Well, to be honest, I'm not used to
carnivores calling me by my name.

95
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:24,668
And I thought that was nice.

96
00:05:32,051 --> 00:05:34,261
[indistinct chatter]

97
00:05:37,431 --> 00:05:40,642
I heard some senior drank
one of those things. He lost it!

98
00:05:40,726 --> 00:05:42,728
And he wound up biting
his girlfriend's finger off.

99
00:05:42,811 --> 00:05:45,272
- No way that's real!
- It was on the news and everything, dude.

100
00:05:45,355 --> 00:05:46,398
It's true!

101
00:05:46,482 --> 00:05:49,193
But, hey, you can try it
if you don't believe me.

102
00:05:49,276 --> 00:05:51,445
You know what? I don't think
I want to push my luck.

103
00:05:51,528 --> 00:05:53,489
Man, don't be a baby!

104
00:05:54,073 --> 00:05:55,866
- Try it.
- [hesitates] Uh...

105
00:05:56,450 --> 00:05:57,367
[grunts]

106
00:05:59,745 --> 00:06:02,164
Huh? This sucker's empty!

107
00:06:02,247 --> 00:06:03,916
- [laughing]
- [can clanging]

108
00:06:03,999 --> 00:06:05,250
What is with you, dude?

109
00:06:06,168 --> 00:06:07,628
Can't stand you sometimes!

110
00:06:07,711 --> 00:06:08,545
[both] Huh?

111
00:06:12,049 --> 00:06:13,717
[both] Uh...

112
00:06:13,801 --> 00:06:16,762
Ah, if it isn't the little lord.

113
00:06:16,845 --> 00:06:19,598
Forgive our rudeness,
it shan't happen again!

114
00:06:19,681 --> 00:06:21,850
- [hyena laughs]
- I'll throw it out for you.

115
00:06:22,476 --> 00:06:24,686
- Nah, it's cool. I got it.
- [hyena laughing]

116
00:06:24,770 --> 00:06:26,313
We're just yanking your horns.

117
00:06:26,396 --> 00:06:29,274
We'd get kicked out of school
if we actually tried to mess with ya.

118
00:06:29,358 --> 00:06:31,193
[hyena] Plus, piss off
The Horns Conglomerate,

119
00:06:31,276 --> 00:06:33,695
and you can say goodbye
to a decent job anywhere.

120
00:06:34,404 --> 00:06:35,989
[lion] Anyway, I'll take that.

121
00:06:38,575 --> 00:06:40,077
I said, give it here!

122
00:06:41,370 --> 00:06:42,746
Meat intoxication?

123
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:44,248
[gasps]

124
00:06:44,331 --> 00:06:46,708
Those withdrawal symptoms are nasty.

125
00:06:48,418 --> 00:06:51,004
- Is this what's causing them?
- I said, give it back!

126
00:06:52,089 --> 00:06:53,215
[lion grunts, strains]

127
00:06:53,298 --> 00:06:56,760
[Louis] <i>Truly an underhanded way
to take a carnivore off their feet.</i>

128
00:06:56,844 --> 00:06:58,262
[strains, yelps]

129
00:06:58,345 --> 00:06:59,179
[grunts]

130
00:07:00,973 --> 00:07:03,892
[Louis] <i>A little trick I picked up
from the Shishi-Gumi.</i>

131
00:07:04,935 --> 00:07:09,815
Listen up. A lion's strength
is a weapon that must be honed.

132
00:07:09,898 --> 00:07:11,817
Don't misuse it, lest it chip.

133
00:07:12,401 --> 00:07:15,487
[growling]

134
00:07:19,658 --> 00:07:20,742
{\an8}Oh, wow.

135
00:07:21,785 --> 00:07:23,203
{\an8}It's kind of elegant.

136
00:07:24,121 --> 00:07:26,415
{\an8}Surely, it doesn't hurt anymore, right?

137
00:07:26,999 --> 00:07:29,460
{\an8}[Louis] It hasn't been
nearly as bad as I thought.

138
00:07:31,253 --> 00:07:33,672
{\an8}I don't exactly understand
why you're showing me.

139
00:07:35,507 --> 00:07:39,470
You're the only one who knows I was ever
in the Black Market in the first place.

140
00:07:39,553 --> 00:07:41,555
I don't know, maybe that's all it is.

141
00:07:42,806 --> 00:07:44,850
It makes sense
you just want someone to know.

142
00:07:44,933 --> 00:07:45,767
Well--

143
00:07:45,851 --> 00:07:47,978
If you're worried about it,
though, that's okay.

144
00:07:48,061 --> 00:07:50,189
[hesitates] I don't care.

145
00:07:50,856 --> 00:07:53,650
Deer shed their antlers
once a year, every year,

146
00:07:53,734 --> 00:07:55,861
so you'll understand
we're not the type to make a fuss

147
00:07:55,944 --> 00:07:57,571
over losing parts of our bodies.

148
00:07:57,654 --> 00:07:58,489
Besides--

149
00:07:59,781 --> 00:08:02,576
[romantic guitar music playing]

150
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,973
[Juno gasps softly] Uh...

151
00:08:25,807 --> 00:08:28,769
[hesitates] I... I don't know why I...

152
00:08:30,062 --> 00:08:33,440
Oh, my gosh, I'm so sorry!
Why did-- I shouldn't--

153
00:08:33,524 --> 00:08:36,652
- Can we just pretend that didn't happen--
- Don't freak out. It never happened.

154
00:08:36,735 --> 00:08:39,238
It-- Hang on a second!
You can't forget it that easily!

155
00:08:39,321 --> 00:08:41,156
- I just gave you my first kiss ever!
- Hey!

156
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,533
- Would you calm down?
- Calm down?

157
00:08:42,616 --> 00:08:46,578
You kissed me because you wanted
to show mercy to a poor injured herbivore.

158
00:08:47,287 --> 00:08:48,705
This conversation is over.

159
00:08:50,457 --> 00:08:52,501
Why would you say something like that?

160
00:08:53,627 --> 00:08:55,629
That really hurts my feelings.

161
00:08:55,712 --> 00:08:58,966
[sighs] I, uh, hope all is well
with the club activities.

162
00:09:07,474 --> 00:09:09,518
<i>There is no good to be found
in falling in love</i>

163
00:09:09,601 --> 00:09:11,436
<i>with someone from another species.</i>

164
00:09:13,063 --> 00:09:14,481
<i>So why am I...</i>

165
00:09:15,274 --> 00:09:16,858
- [sighs]
- [indistinct chatter]

166
00:09:16,942 --> 00:09:19,903
[Louis] <i>I thought I had severed
my ties with the carnivores.</i>

167
00:09:19,987 --> 00:09:21,905
<i>Why can't I seem to shake them off?</i>

168
00:09:22,573 --> 00:09:23,782
[scoffs]

169
00:09:23,865 --> 00:09:25,284
[indistinct chatter]

170
00:09:25,909 --> 00:09:27,786
- [thudding]
- [footstep thuds]

171
00:09:28,787 --> 00:09:30,455
- [can cracks open]
- [drink fizzes]

172
00:09:36,295 --> 00:09:37,379
[sighs]

173
00:09:38,338 --> 00:09:39,256
[exhales]

174
00:09:39,798 --> 00:09:41,174
[inhales deeply]

175
00:09:42,593 --> 00:09:43,844
[exhales]

176
00:09:43,927 --> 00:09:45,345
[laughs]

177
00:09:48,307 --> 00:09:50,309
[gulping]

178
00:09:50,392 --> 00:09:53,270
[ominous music playing]

179
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:57,190
[sighs contentedly, laughs]

180
00:09:58,817 --> 00:09:59,735
Huh?

181
00:10:00,569 --> 00:10:01,820
[gasps]

182
00:10:03,572 --> 00:10:05,741
[gagging]

183
00:10:07,784 --> 00:10:09,995
[straining]

184
00:10:12,331 --> 00:10:14,333
[breathing heavily]

185
00:10:15,292 --> 00:10:17,294
[growling]

186
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,465
[train rattling]

187
00:10:28,013 --> 00:10:30,057
[footsteps approaching]

188
00:10:32,851 --> 00:10:35,646
How long you want to bet
this guy's going to keep us waiting?

189
00:10:35,729 --> 00:10:39,149
Right? And after all that talk
about rebranding us too!

190
00:10:39,232 --> 00:10:41,068
- [clanking]
- [both] Hmm?

191
00:10:42,486 --> 00:10:44,613
[Free] Huh? What is that?

192
00:10:46,698 --> 00:10:47,741
- Hmm.
- Huh?

193
00:10:49,242 --> 00:10:50,118
[both] Hmm.

194
00:10:50,202 --> 00:10:52,245
- [low growling]
- [Free] Hmm?

195
00:10:58,043 --> 00:11:00,045
[suspenseful music playing]

196
00:11:01,588 --> 00:11:02,464
Jimma?

197
00:11:03,674 --> 00:11:05,676
[growling]

198
00:11:09,388 --> 00:11:11,515
[growling]

199
00:11:14,476 --> 00:11:16,019
Stop! What's your deal?

200
00:11:16,645 --> 00:11:19,940
[all grunting]

201
00:11:25,529 --> 00:11:27,739
[Agata] Calm down! What's wrong with you?

202
00:11:28,532 --> 00:11:30,325
- That's it. [grunts]
- [Jimma groans]

203
00:11:31,952 --> 00:11:33,203
[Jimma breathing heavily]

204
00:11:33,286 --> 00:11:36,665
[Free] You dumbass.
What the hell were you thinking?

205
00:11:36,748 --> 00:11:38,375
[Dolph] Who put you up to this?

206
00:11:38,458 --> 00:11:40,627
[groans] I don't know...

207
00:11:41,128 --> 00:11:42,462
Yeah, right.

208
00:11:42,546 --> 00:11:44,589
[heavy footsteps approaching]

209
00:11:44,673 --> 00:11:46,216
[all] Hmm?

210
00:11:50,262 --> 00:11:51,096
Is that him?

211
00:11:51,805 --> 00:11:55,392
[Melon] You should know better
than to get high on your own supply.

212
00:11:55,475 --> 00:11:59,271
What? You make it sound like
we're drug dealers or something.

213
00:12:01,064 --> 00:12:03,900
[Dolph] This isn't
a regular energy drink I'm guessing.

214
00:12:05,986 --> 00:12:09,656
[Melon] Kines contains
the flesh and bones of herbivores.

215
00:12:09,739 --> 00:12:11,658
Though admittedly only a small amount,

216
00:12:11,741 --> 00:12:15,078
it's just enough to satisfy
a meat craving.

217
00:12:15,662 --> 00:12:17,998
Give you a little extra boost of vitality.

218
00:12:18,081 --> 00:12:19,583
[footsteps thudding]

219
00:12:19,666 --> 00:12:24,588
But if you drink too much,
one day, it won't be enough.

220
00:12:25,547 --> 00:12:30,093
That's when they come to the Black Market,
seeking real meat.

221
00:12:30,719 --> 00:12:34,097
So, thanks to the Shishi-Gumi,
Black Market business is booming.

222
00:12:35,098 --> 00:12:37,684
[Melon] Unfortunately,
when someone drinks it,

223
00:12:37,767 --> 00:12:40,145
who's experienced the real thing...

224
00:12:42,189 --> 00:12:43,023
Well...

225
00:12:43,523 --> 00:12:45,567
[Free] Yeah, I get it.

226
00:12:46,902 --> 00:12:48,987
[Jimma groans softly] Huh?

227
00:12:51,781 --> 00:12:52,616
[all] Huh?

228
00:12:52,699 --> 00:12:54,493
[Melon] Deliver it to this address.

229
00:12:54,576 --> 00:12:58,580
"Gardona and Algama... Center Street"?

230
00:12:59,289 --> 00:13:01,750
You want us to go out
and sell this mainstream?

231
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:04,419
[Melon] Oh, no, no, no. Just deliver it.

232
00:13:05,295 --> 00:13:08,798
Your hideous faces
couldn't sell water to a fish.

233
00:13:09,341 --> 00:13:11,801
- We haven't agreed to do it yet!
- [both] Huh?

234
00:13:12,385 --> 00:13:14,471
You found a single piece of ivory.

235
00:13:14,554 --> 00:13:17,015
It'll take more than that
for you to be the boss.

236
00:13:17,849 --> 00:13:20,143
[Melon] Oh. I guess you have a point.

237
00:13:20,227 --> 00:13:21,061
[loud clamp]

238
00:13:23,188 --> 00:13:24,856
- [heavy thud]
- [gasps]

239
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,149
[all gasping]

240
00:13:26,233 --> 00:13:27,275
[Melon] How's this?

241
00:13:27,734 --> 00:13:29,444
[lions breath trembling]

242
00:13:31,363 --> 00:13:33,073
[car horns honking]

243
00:13:39,663 --> 00:13:42,415
[leopard] Look who it is!
Hey, Little Lamb!

244
00:13:42,499 --> 00:13:44,876
Inspecting the sales floor on a day off?

245
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:47,796
Yeah, ever the diligent employee, I see.

246
00:13:47,879 --> 00:13:50,799
Well, turns out, so are we. [laughs]

247
00:13:50,882 --> 00:13:53,969
[Seven] <i>Ugh! It's just my luck
to run into these two.</i>

248
00:13:54,052 --> 00:13:55,971
<i>What a waste of a lovely day.</i>

249
00:13:56,054 --> 00:13:58,431
The herbivore department's
been on fire lately,

250
00:13:58,515 --> 00:14:00,183
so I'd say you've earned a little break.

251
00:14:00,267 --> 00:14:02,018
[chuckles] Yes, maybe you're right.

252
00:14:02,852 --> 00:14:05,313
<i>But no matter, I can deal with them
easily enough.</i>

253
00:14:05,397 --> 00:14:07,941
<i>A fake smile always seems to do the trick.</i>

254
00:14:08,024 --> 00:14:10,360
We carnivores have a harder time selling.

255
00:14:10,443 --> 00:14:11,570
But all you've got to do

256
00:14:11,653 --> 00:14:14,030
- is flash those pearly whites of yours.
- [Legoshi] Hey, uh...

257
00:14:14,614 --> 00:14:16,116
- [Seven] Hmm?
- [leopard] Huh?

258
00:14:17,409 --> 00:14:20,579
Sorry, these are a little small.

259
00:14:20,662 --> 00:14:23,707
[both trembling]

260
00:14:24,541 --> 00:14:26,751
- This guy a friend of yours?
- [Seven] Huh?

261
00:14:26,835 --> 00:14:28,253
[Legoshi] I'm her neighbor.

262
00:14:29,045 --> 00:14:32,799
[laughs] You had me going there!
Thought he was the boyfriend.

263
00:14:32,883 --> 00:14:35,218
- No, just the neighbor.
- [Seven chuckling] Oh, goodness no.

264
00:14:35,302 --> 00:14:38,096
And this lady's name is Ms. Seven,
by the way.

265
00:14:38,179 --> 00:14:39,639
- [gasps]
- Not "Little Lamb."

266
00:14:40,557 --> 00:14:42,642
Unless that's, like,
a work nickname? I don't know.

267
00:14:42,726 --> 00:14:44,227
Yeah, it's... it's a nickname.

268
00:14:44,311 --> 00:14:46,479
Just a little joke
between coworkers, right?

269
00:14:46,563 --> 00:14:47,814
CLEARANCE SALE. 5300 YEN

270
00:14:47,898 --> 00:14:52,360
[leopard] Uh, sure, yeah.
We didn't mean anything by it.

271
00:14:52,444 --> 00:14:54,362
- [hesitates] Uh...
- [sighs]

272
00:14:54,446 --> 00:14:57,240
Uh, now that I think about it,
it's way too mean.

273
00:14:57,324 --> 00:14:58,950
Who even started that? You?

274
00:14:59,034 --> 00:15:00,994
Uh, no, no! It was the boss.

275
00:15:01,077 --> 00:15:04,247
Uh, anyway, sorry to bother you.
We should get going.

276
00:15:04,331 --> 00:15:06,666
[sighs] We'll see you around, Ms. Seven.

277
00:15:07,918 --> 00:15:09,294
[Seven] <i>What just happened?</i>

278
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:14,716
<i>All these years, I've had to put up
with these bullies, and now they just...</i>

279
00:15:14,799 --> 00:15:15,967
[Legoshi] Are you okay?

280
00:15:16,676 --> 00:15:18,845
It looked like
they had you cornered there.

281
00:15:19,763 --> 00:15:21,556
[Seven] <i>Just because he's...</i>

282
00:15:23,558 --> 00:15:25,769
So, I suppose you think you've saved me?

283
00:15:25,852 --> 00:15:27,354
[stutters]

284
00:15:30,065 --> 00:15:32,734
- [tires screech]
- [Legoshi] Hey, wait! I'm sorry!

285
00:15:32,817 --> 00:15:35,278
Are you upset because those guys thought
I was your boyfriend?

286
00:15:35,362 --> 00:15:36,947
'Cause I tried to tell them.

287
00:15:37,030 --> 00:15:38,782
[Seven sighs] <i>Unbelievable!</i>

288
00:15:38,865 --> 00:15:41,117
<i>He really is just a little kid!</i>

289
00:15:41,201 --> 00:15:43,286
<i>- He's a child!</i>
- [Legoshi chatters indistinctly]

290
00:15:44,496 --> 00:15:46,915
Tell me, why is it that someone like you
has more authority

291
00:15:46,998 --> 00:15:48,708
- in the social hierarchy than I do?
- Huh?

292
00:15:48,792 --> 00:15:50,794
You're not even a functioning adult yet,

293
00:15:50,877 --> 00:15:52,963
and you still managed
to shut them up in seconds

294
00:15:53,046 --> 00:15:54,881
without so much as a courtesy smile!

295
00:15:55,465 --> 00:15:58,051
And how? By being a great, big carnivore?

296
00:15:58,134 --> 00:15:59,469
You better watch it, wolf!

297
00:15:59,552 --> 00:16:01,513
- I'll report you!
- [Legoshi chuckles nervously]

298
00:16:01,596 --> 00:16:04,516
[Seven] Oh, no, that's okay.
[chuckles nervously, sighs]

299
00:16:04,599 --> 00:16:06,685
[amusing music playing]

300
00:16:08,103 --> 00:16:10,063
{\an8}[Legoshi] <i>I didn't even consider that.</i>

301
00:16:10,939 --> 00:16:15,193
{\an8}<i>She's been treated in ways
I've never had to experience before.</i>

302
00:16:16,444 --> 00:16:17,612
<i>And maybe never will.</i>

303
00:16:18,863 --> 00:16:20,115
[pops]

304
00:16:21,866 --> 00:16:24,577
[gulping]

305
00:16:25,495 --> 00:16:27,247
[sighs contentedly]

306
00:16:28,331 --> 00:16:30,000
- [Legoshi] Ms. Seven?
- Huh?

307
00:16:30,875 --> 00:16:34,921
{\an8}What, so you're following me now?
Leave me alone so I can drink in peace!

308
00:16:35,672 --> 00:16:40,260
[Legoshi] I'm sorry. I acted
without thinking, and that was rude.

309
00:16:41,970 --> 00:16:44,389
[sighs] Just let it go.

310
00:16:45,265 --> 00:16:46,850
You'll learn as you get older.

311
00:16:46,933 --> 00:16:49,394
It feels miserable when you want
an apology from someone

312
00:16:49,477 --> 00:16:51,229
and they actually give it to you.

313
00:16:52,063 --> 00:16:53,356
Then, what do I say?

314
00:16:54,983 --> 00:16:56,943
- You don't have to say anything at all.
- Huh?

315
00:16:57,527 --> 00:17:00,530
I'm not upset with you.
You did nothing wrong.

316
00:17:02,866 --> 00:17:04,951
Should I not respond to that either, or...

317
00:17:05,035 --> 00:17:07,537
[chuckles] You need to relax a little.

318
00:17:09,164 --> 00:17:10,081
[cans thud softly]

319
00:17:13,793 --> 00:17:15,795
- [boat engine whirring]
- [horn blares]

320
00:17:20,383 --> 00:17:21,801
[black panther] Mmm.

321
00:17:22,886 --> 00:17:27,015
If you pocketed a stack of cash or two,
what would you eat with it?

322
00:17:27,098 --> 00:17:30,018
Don't make jokes like that.
You'll get yourself killed.

323
00:17:30,101 --> 00:17:32,228
- [squeaking, chattering]
- Huh?

324
00:17:32,312 --> 00:17:35,607
[mysterious music playing]

325
00:17:40,403 --> 00:17:43,573
- [gasps softly]
- Hmm? Is that Gohin?

326
00:17:48,411 --> 00:17:52,582
It's not Gohin.
It's The 500 Cornered Rats!

327
00:17:52,665 --> 00:17:54,334
[yells in pain]

328
00:17:54,417 --> 00:17:56,503
- [whimpering]
- Jeez, are you all right?

329
00:17:57,629 --> 00:18:00,256
[gasps] Hey, hold it!
You wait right there!

330
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:03,843
Uh... They're splitting up! What do we do?
That's Shishi-Gumi money!

331
00:18:03,927 --> 00:18:05,303
You think I don't know that?

332
00:18:05,386 --> 00:18:06,471
[rats chittering]

333
00:18:06,554 --> 00:18:09,015
[rats exclaim, squeak excitedly]

334
00:18:11,851 --> 00:18:15,271
- [Corne] Toodle-oo!
- [pants, grunts in frustration]

335
00:18:15,355 --> 00:18:18,274
- [rats squeaking]
- [grunting, indistinct shouting]

336
00:18:19,859 --> 00:18:24,197
[Corne] <i>We are The 500 Cornered Rats.
We steal from the bad people.</i>

337
00:18:24,906 --> 00:18:26,699
<i>By mobilizing our huge base,</i>

338
00:18:26,783 --> 00:18:30,537
<i>we can influence not only
the Black Market economy, but everybody.</i>

339
00:18:31,579 --> 00:18:33,790
<i>Got to admit, the job's got its perks.</i>

340
00:18:33,873 --> 00:18:36,417
[chittering]

341
00:18:39,712 --> 00:18:41,256
[grunting]

342
00:18:42,173 --> 00:18:43,883
[indistinct shouting]

343
00:18:45,969 --> 00:18:47,262
- [grunts]
- [rats groan]

344
00:18:52,142 --> 00:18:55,728
It was you filthy rats that stole
the mayor's gold watch, wasn't it?

345
00:18:55,812 --> 00:18:58,398
- Spill it!
- [grunting]

346
00:19:00,150 --> 00:19:02,861
[officer] We're the police,
and even we couldn't care less

347
00:19:02,944 --> 00:19:05,446
if a bunch of punk rats just up and died.

348
00:19:09,367 --> 00:19:11,703
No, no, all lives are equal.

349
00:19:12,453 --> 00:19:13,913
- [both gasp]
- Mr. Yahya!

350
00:19:14,414 --> 00:19:18,668
Larger species like you
that tower over a lot of the other ones,

351
00:19:18,751 --> 00:19:22,672
species so small,
they can't even trigger automatic doors,

352
00:19:22,755 --> 00:19:24,007
and even yours truly...

353
00:19:25,425 --> 00:19:26,676
We're all the same...

354
00:19:27,635 --> 00:19:30,221
Every species equally insignificant.

355
00:19:31,764 --> 00:19:37,979
And saving those poor insignificant lives
is my charge for better or worse.

356
00:19:41,816 --> 00:19:43,484
Those jerks! [groans]

357
00:19:43,568 --> 00:19:45,236
Just because we're rats. [groans]

358
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:48,031
Sounds like a case
of making your own bed, I'm afraid.

359
00:19:48,865 --> 00:19:50,742
So, any new ideas?

360
00:19:51,618 --> 00:19:54,704
Well, it's not Doku-Gumi, Inari-Gumi,
or Madara-Gumi.

361
00:19:55,246 --> 00:19:57,415
No other leads so far.

362
00:19:57,498 --> 00:20:00,210
- And what about Shishi-Gumi?
- Can't be them.

363
00:20:00,293 --> 00:20:01,794
Without a stable leader,

364
00:20:01,878 --> 00:20:05,131
Shishi-Gumi wouldn't be able
to handle something like Kines.

365
00:20:05,757 --> 00:20:10,303
And, unfortunately, it's available
way more than we anticipated.

366
00:20:10,386 --> 00:20:11,387
UDON BEBEBE

367
00:20:11,471 --> 00:20:14,015
[Yahya] <i>It's circulating
in mainstream society now?</i>

368
00:20:14,098 --> 00:20:15,558
[Legoshi] Anyway, good night.

369
00:20:16,434 --> 00:20:17,727
[Corne] <i>Damn straight.</i>

370
00:20:17,810 --> 00:20:19,187
<i>And, apparently, young carnivores</i>

371
00:20:19,270 --> 00:20:22,190
<i>have been getting their hands
on this stuff pretty quickly.</i>

372
00:20:23,066 --> 00:20:25,193
[Yahya] <i>According
to the forensic analysis,</i>

373
00:20:25,276 --> 00:20:28,696
<i>it appears to contain
several narcotic-like components.</i>

374
00:20:29,656 --> 00:20:31,324
<i>Those most at risk are carnivores</i>

375
00:20:31,407 --> 00:20:34,035
<i>with previous experience
of meat consumption.</i>

376
00:20:35,203 --> 00:20:38,706
<i>Apparently, even a single dose
can induce side effects,</i>

377
00:20:38,790 --> 00:20:43,044
<i>which include a strong craving for meat
and increased aggressiveness.</i>

378
00:20:45,672 --> 00:20:48,758
[Legoshi] <i>It's the first money
I've ever earned on my own.</i>

379
00:20:49,342 --> 00:20:51,928
<i>I should pay the rent
and my electric bills first,</i>

380
00:20:52,011 --> 00:20:54,264
<i>but then, flowers for Haru.</i>

381
00:20:55,473 --> 00:20:57,767
<i>I think I'm going to do well
for myself here.</i>

382
00:20:58,851 --> 00:21:02,188
<i>So, I want to make sure
I do right by Haru too.</i>

383
00:21:02,897 --> 00:21:03,982
<i>No more secrets.</i>

384
00:21:07,986 --> 00:21:11,781
Hey, young man!
Excuse me, hello. Good evening, sir.

385
00:21:11,864 --> 00:21:13,283
Hi, good evening.

386
00:21:13,366 --> 00:21:15,535
[black panther chuckles wickedly] Mmm.

387
00:21:15,618 --> 00:21:18,037
{\an8}How would you like to try
a special energy drink,

388
00:21:18,121 --> 00:21:19,205
{\an8}just for carnivores?

389
00:21:20,081 --> 00:21:22,083
You seem very tired this evening.

390
00:21:22,792 --> 00:21:25,378
And it seems like the people out there
pushing this stuff

391
00:21:25,461 --> 00:21:27,755
have no clue about those side effects.

392
00:21:29,132 --> 00:21:31,551
If we're not very careful,

393
00:21:31,634 --> 00:21:35,388
before too long, we could have carnivores
killing each other in the streets.

394
00:21:36,764 --> 00:21:39,851
Uh, I'm okay. I have more stamina
than you would think.

395
00:21:39,934 --> 00:21:42,854
Nah, come on, come on.
Just trust me, you'll love it.

396
00:21:42,937 --> 00:21:45,231
{\an8}You can try one, it won't hurt.

397
00:21:45,315 --> 00:21:46,399
{\an8}[drink fizzes]

398
00:21:47,066 --> 00:21:47,900
Hmm?

399
00:21:50,403 --> 00:21:53,156
<i>Mmm...</i>

400
00:21:54,782 --> 00:21:56,784
[soft growling]

401
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

402
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,792
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

403
00:22:04,876 --> 00:22:08,296
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

404
00:22:09,464 --> 00:22:12,508
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

405
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,762
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

406
00:22:17,805 --> 00:22:20,516
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

407
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,561
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

408
00:22:23,644 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

409
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,569
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

410
00:22:32,612 --> 00:22:36,824
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

411
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

412
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,791
<i>- ♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

413
00:22:44,874 --> 00:22:46,793
<i>- ♪ Till I... ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

414
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,002
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

415
00:22:48,086 --> 00:22:52,590
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

416
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

417
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,765
<i>- ♪ Just want to feel like this ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

418
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:02,809
<i>- ♪ Till the... ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

419
00:23:02,892 --> 00:23:04,102
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

420
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:09,148
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

421
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

422
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,693
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

423
00:23:13,444 --> 00:23:16,322
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

424
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:19,325
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

425
00:23:19,408 --> 00:23:24,330
{\an8}<i>-♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪
- ♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

426
00:23:25,414 --> 00:23:28,876
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪
- ♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
